a(1709,'duty-rms','Duty-cycle copper-loss check','A declared constant-flux motor with K_t=0.10 N m/A and R=2 Ω alternates 0.60 N m for 2 s and 0.20 N m for 6 s. Ignoring transients and other losses, what is its mean copper loss over the cycle?', [('24 W.','Use time-weighted squared current, not squared mean current.'),('18 W.','This squares the 3 A mean current instead of averaging I².'),('40 W.','This averages the two loss levels equally despite unequal durations.'),('72 W.','This is only the high-torque segment loss, not the cycle average.')], 'A duty cycle can change heating even when a peak torque is briefly feasible; this is a simplified loss estimate, not thermal approval.',loc='Operating duty cycle selection factor and distinct continuous/peak torque envelopes.',kind='figure',typ='numerical',diff='medium',steps=['I_high=0.60/0.10=6 A; I_low=0.20/0.10=2 A.','Mean I²=(2×36+6×4)/8=12 A².','Mean copper loss=R×12=24 W.'],forms=[DC,PWR,formula('P̄_cu=R Σ(I_j² t_j)/Σt_j',{'P̄_cu':'cycle-average copper loss','R':'constant armature resistance','I_j':'current in segment j','t_j':'duration of segment j','j':'cycle segment index'},{'P̄_cu':'W','R':'Ω','I_j':'A','t_j':'s','j':'dimensionless'},['Added piecewise-steady duty cycle; resistance constant; no cooling model or transient loss.'])],assumptions=['Added two-segment cycle and motor constants; no hardware operation or continuous-duty certification.'])
a([1693,1699],'field-weakening','Declared field-weakening tradeoff','For an added unsaturated field-wound model, halve flux while keeping supply voltage fixed and neglecting armature resistive drop. If both K_t and K_v scale with flux, how do ideal no-load speed and current for the same nonzero torque change?', [('Both double.','Speed is V/K_v; fixed torque requires I=T/K_t.'),('Speed doubles and required current halves.','The current dependence on K_t is inverse for fixed torque.'),('Speed halves and required current doubles.','The no-load speed is inversely related to K_v.'),('Both stay unchanged.','Both specified coefficients change with flux.')], 'This explicitly supplied model develops the source’s field-current speed-control statement; thermal and commutation limits may prevent the ideal target.',loc={1693:'T=Kt I and Vb=Kvω coefficient relations.',1699:'Field-wound speed can be varied by armature or field current statement.'},kind={1693:'equation',1699:'statement'},typ='numerical',diff='medium',steps=['K_t,new=K_t/2 and K_v,new=K_v/2.','ω_0,new=V/(K_v/2)=2ω_0.','I_new=T/(K_t/2)=2I for the same torque.'],forms=[DC],assumptions=['Added linear unsaturated flux scaling; ideal no-load speed calculation ignores resistive drop, while separate same-torque current comparison is electromagnetic.'])
