a([1694,1709],'stall-power','Stall torque and mechanical power','Under an added ideal steady DC model, Assertion: a stalled motor can produce nonzero electromagnetic torque while delivering zero shaft mechanical power. Reason: shaft mechanical power is torque multiplied by angular speed. Which option is correct?', [('Both statements are true, and the reason explains the assertion.','At stall ω=0, so Tω=0 even when T is nonzero.'),('Both are true, but the reason is unrelated to the assertion.','The product relation directly explains it.'),('The assertion is true, but the reason is false.','The stated mechanical-power relation is correct.'),('The assertion is false, but the reason is true.','Nonzero torque at zero speed is allowed; zero power does not imply zero torque.')], 'Stall can still draw electrical current and generate heating; zero shaft power is not safe continuous operation.',loc={1694:'Starting ω=0 torque proportional to voltage and current relation.',1709:'Starting torque, power and duty-cycle selection factors.'},kind={1694:'equation',1709:'statement'},typ='assertion_reason',forms=[DC,PWR],assumptions=['Added ideal steady model, no instantaneous inductive current jump assumed.'])
